A student will have committed a breach of discipline or an act of general misconduct if the student:
Behaves in a manner which is detrimental to the interests and good repute of the University.
Harasses any person on any grounds, including ethincity, gender, sexual preference or religious or political belief;
Engages in threating/pressurising Faculty Members and /or Officers of the University inside or outside the university premises;
Engages in creating disturbance in the Class Rooms/Laboratories;
Engages in creating Law and order situation in the University premises;
Will-fully, recklessly or negligently engages in conduct which causes, or may cause, bodily injury to any person;
Engages in improper use of any University facilities or equipment;
